WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.834
-You guys, we have been so happy

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.400
to have Fred Armisen
with us all week.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.400
Fred, how are you, my friend?
-I'm doing great.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.267
-It's so exciting
to have you here for a week

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:09.601
and this is really
exciting, too --

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.667
it is Opening Day
in Major League Baseball.

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:12.934
I know you're a huge sports fan,

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:15.367
a huge baseball fan, huge.
-Huge, huge. Baseball.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.033
[ Laughter ]
-Which team do you think
has the best chances?

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.534
-Phillies.
-Great.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.634
[ Cheering and applause ]
Phillies all the way.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.801
-Phillies everywhere.
But I also heard --

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.734
is this true --
that you are launching,

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:28.667
next week is the opening day
of your rival baseball league?

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.501
-Yes.
-That's so exciting.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:33.400
-So I have this baseball league
that is like

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.934
it's players from every team...

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:39.868
-Uh-huh.
-...in both leagues,

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:41.934
National and American.
-Great.

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:43.467
You do know a lot
about baseball.
-I do.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:44.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.968
But it's less about like,

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:47.200
"I'm from this team
or that team."

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.934
It's more like a crowd
of players on the field.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.267
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.
-Right?

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.601
And it's more like
let's have fun.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.200
Let's throw a bunch
of baseballs around.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.801
[ Laughter ]
Like it doesn't have to be
so many rules.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.067
That's like from another time.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.801
Let's all just enjoy
this moment.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.000
-Okay.
-So --

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.467
-So it's just a bunch of guys
on the field,

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.400
throwing balls around?

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.400
-Yeah, but in a way
that's like sort of, you know,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.901
with enjoyment.
-Do --

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.167
[ Laughter ]
Is there a way to keep score?

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.901
-Yeah. So, so,
for every three times

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:17.167
that someone catches a ball,
right,

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.133
that's 7 points.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.934
[ Laughter ]
Every fourth time, zero points.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.534
Any fastball that goes
to left field,

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:28.667
where four people catch those,

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.667
10 points, with 5 subtracted,
if it's from the opposing team.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.501
[ Laughter ]
-And that's it.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.601
-Those are the only rules?
-Those are the only rules.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.000
-Wait, how long
does the game take?

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.267
-Five minutes.
-Okay.

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:38.934
-Quickly, yeah.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:42.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.767
-And what is it called,
if we're looking for it?

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.534
-It's just called
regular baseball.

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:47.834
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, great.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.634
-Give it up one more time
for Fred Armisen, everybody.

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:50.968
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Thank you.

